<title>MACEDONIA: Macedonia August industrial output down 1.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Macedonia August industrial output down 1.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SKOPJE 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macedonia's industrial output fell by 1.4 percent in August against July due to a seasonal drop in production related to summer vacation, the National Bank of Macedonia (NBM) said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Output declines in summer months traditionally because of the holiday season,&quot; an NBM official who declined to be named told Reuters.</p>
<p>Compared to August 1995 industrial output rose by 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-328101</p>
